AMM::constructor(address _admin, address _controller, address _strategyManager, address _oracle, uint256 _cw, address _eve, address _exitQueue)
├── Given any constructor argument is zero address
│   └── It should revert with AMMZeroAddress
├── Given valid parameters
│   ├── It should set connectorWeight via _setConnectorWeight and emit ConnectorWeightChanged(0, _cw)
│   ├── It should set minBatchExitETH via _setMinBatchExitETH and emit MinBatchExitETHChanged(0, DEFAULT_MIN_BATCH_EXIT_ETH)
│   ├── It should grant ADMIN_ROLE to _admin
│   └── It should grant CONTROLLER_ROLE to _controller

AMM::enter(uint256 _minTokensToMint) payable
├── Given the caller is not whitelisted (Whitelist.isWhitelisted(msg.sender) == false)
│   └── It should revert with AMMNotWhitelisted (checked before any other enter() logic, including bootstrap)
├── Given the caller is whitelisted (directly by admin, via a previously redeemed invite, or the Whitelist gate is disabled)
│   └── It should proceed exactly as before this check existed
├── When _minTokensToMint is zero
│   └── It should revert with AMMInvalidTokensToMintAmount
├── Given contract is not bootstrapped
│   ├── When ETH deposit is below MIN_INITIAL_DEPOSIT_USD (in USD value)
│   │   └── It should revert with AMMLessThanMinInitialDeposit
│   ├── When deposit covers the minimum but userTokens (depositUSD - _DEAD_SUPPLY) < _minTokensToMint
│   │   └── It should revert with AMMInsufficientDeposit
│   ├── When ETH deposit is sufficient
│   │   ├── It should call oracle to convert ETH to USD for validation
│   │   ├── It should set bootstrapped = true
│   │   ├── It should mint _DEAD_SUPPLY (1e18) to address(0xdead)
│   │   ├── It should mint userTokens (= depositUSD - _DEAD_SUPPLY) to user BEFORE transferring ETH to controller (same CEI as post-bootstrap enter)
│   │   ├── It should set total supply to depositUSD
│   │   ├── It should transfer ETH to controller (via sendValue)
│   │   └── It should emit Bootstrapped event
│   ├── When oracle price is stale (during bootstrap validation)
│   │   └── It should revert with OracleStalePrice
│   └── When oracle price is invalid / zero (during bootstrap validation)
│       └── It should revert (oracle reverts with OracleInvalidPrice)
├── Given contract is bootstrapped
│   ├── When tokensToMint (priced via _evePremiumPriceInETH) < _minTokensToMint
│   │   └── It should revert with AMMInsufficientDeposit
│   └── When ETH deposit is sufficient
│       ├── It should price tokens using premium price in ETH (_evePremiumPriceInETH)
│       ├── It should exclude msg.value from NAV when pricing (pre-deposit NAV)
│       ├── It should not inflate NAV with locked claim ETH
│       ├── It should mint tokens to user (via mint) BEFORE transferring ETH to controller (AMM-3 / CEI)
│       ├── It should transfer ETH to controller (via sendValue)
│       ├── A Controller receive() observer must already see the post-mint totalSupply (mid-call)
│       └── It should emit UserEntered event
└── Given contract is paused
    └── It should revert with EnforcedPause

AMM::enterWithInvite(uint256 _minTokensToMint, bytes32 _inviteId, uint256 _deadline, bytes calldata _signature) payable
├── Given the voucher is invalid (per Whitelist.whitelist(): reused invite, expired deadline,
│   unauthorized signer, or the caller is banned) and the caller is not already whitelisted
│   └── It should revert (bubbling the Whitelist revert) before any enter() logic runs
├── Given the voucher is valid and the caller was not previously whitelisted
│   ├── It should whitelist msg.sender on the protocol Whitelist (as a side effect)
│   ├── It should consume (mark as used) _inviteId
│   └── It should then proceed exactly like enter(_minTokensToMint) (bootstrap or normal mint)
├── Given the caller is already whitelisted (admin, prior invite, or Whitelist.disable())
│   └── It should still proceed to enter() normally (Whitelist.whitelist() is a no-op; voucher left unconsumed)
├── Given the caller is msg.sender for both the voucher and the mint
│   └── A relayer submitting this call cannot redirect the minted EVE to itself (EVE is always minted to msg.sender)
└── Given contract is paused
    └── It should revert with EnforcedPause

AMM::exit(uint256 _requestedETH, uint256 _maxTokensToBurn, uint256 _priceTolerance)
├── Given contract is not bootstrapped
│   └── It should revert with AMMZeroTotalSupply (zero supply during pricing)
├── Given contract is bootstrapped
│   ├── When _requestedETH is zero
│   │   └── It should revert with AMMZeroETHRequested
│   ├── When _maxTokensToBurn is zero
│   │   └── It should revert with AMMZeroTokensToBurnAmount
│   ├── When _priceTolerance is greater than Math.SCALE_FACTOR (1e18)
│   │   └── It should revert with AMMInvalidRange
│   ├── When calculating tokensToBurn and ethToRedeem
│   │   └── It should use the live base price in ETH (NAV−L / liveSupply via _basePriceFromNAV)
│   ├── When tokensToBurn calculation results in zero
│   │   └── It should revert with AMMTooLowETHRequested
│   ├── When _maxTokensToBurn is less than calculated tokensToBurn
│   │   └── It should revert with AMMTooMuchETHRequested
│   ├── When free balance is sufficient (freeBalance() >= ethToRedeem)
│   │   ├── It should price the burn using base price in ETH (_eveBasePriceInETH)
│   │   ├── It should size the burn against NAV including AMM free balance
│   │   ├── It should burn tokens from user (via burnFrom)
│   │   ├── It should transfer ETH to user (via sendValue)
│   │   ├── It should emit RedeemedImmediately event
│   │   ├── It should return 0 (no batch ID, processed immediately)
│   │   ├── It should NOT queue redemption
│   │   └── It should NOT enforce minBatchExitETH (immediate exit has no minimum)
│   ├── When free balance is insufficient (freeBalance() < ethToRedeem)
│   │   ├── When ethToRedeem is below minBatchExitETH
│   │   │   └── It should revert with AMMTooLowBatchExitETH
│   │   ├── When ethToRedeem is at or above minBatchExitETH
│   │   │   ├── It should transfer tokens from user to AMM contract (via safeTransferFrom)
│   │   │   ├── It should call exitQueue.pushRequest() to queue redemption
│   │   │   ├── It should emit RedemptionQueued event (with batchId)
│   │   │   ├── It should return batchId (non-zero)
│   │   │   ├── It should NOT transfer ETH immediately
│   │   │   ├── It should NOT call oracle (exit uses ETH prices directly)
│   │   │   └── It should use freeBalance() (not total balance) so locked claims are excluded
│   │   └── When minBatchExitETH is zero (admin disabled)
│   │       └── It should allow queuing sub-minimum ethToRedeem amounts
│   └── When contract is paused
│       └── It should revert with EnforcedPause
├── Given caller does not have CONTROLLER_ROLE (exit is public)
│   └── It should allow execution (exit doesn't require CONTROLLER_ROLE)
└── Given caller is not whitelisted
    └── It should still succeed (exit() never consults the Whitelist — users can always leave)

AMM::processRedemption(uint256 _batchId, address _user) payable
├── Given caller does not have CONTROLLER_ROLE
│   └── It should revert with AccessControlUnauthorizedAccount
├── Given batch ID does not exist or user not in batch
│   └── It should revert (ExitQueue reverts)
├── Given request is already processed
│   └── It should revert (ExitQueue reverts)
├── Given request was closed due to slippage (closedDueToSlippage == true)
│   ├── It should call exitQueue.pullRequest()
│   ├── It should refund tokens to user (via safeTransfer)
│   ├── It should return all sent ETH (msg.value) to controller (via sendValue)
│   ├── It should NOT credit claimableBalances or update lockedForClaims
│   └── It should emit RedemptionProcessed event
└── Given request is within price tolerance (sufficient ETH sent)
    ├── It should call exitQueue.pullRequest() to mark as processed
    ├── It should burn tokens from AMM (via burn)
    ├── It should calculate ethToRedeem from finalEvePrice (via batchInfo)
    ├── It should credit ethToRedeem to claimableBalances[user] (pull-over-push, not direct transfer)
    ├── It should increment lockedForClaims by ethToRedeem
    ├── It should return excess ETH (msg.value - ethToRedeem) to controller
    └── It should emit RedemptionProcessed event

AMM::claim()
├── Given caller has no claimable balance (claimableBalances[msg.sender] == 0)
│   └── It should revert with AMMNoClaimableBalance
├── Given caller has a claimable balance
│   ├── It should transfer claimableETH to msg.sender (via sendValue)
│   ├── It should set claimableBalances[msg.sender] to zero
│   ├── It should decrement lockedForClaims by claimableETH
│   └── It should emit Claimed event
└── Given contract is paused
    └── It should still succeed (claim is not gated by whenNotPaused)

AMM::cancelRedemption(uint256 _batchId)
├── Given batch ID does not exist or user not in batch
│   └── It should revert with ExitQueueRequestNotInBatch
├── Given caller is not the request owner
│   └── It should revert with ExitQueueRequestNotInBatch
├── Given request is already processed
│   └── It should revert (ExitQueue reverts)
├── Given batch is priced and within MAX_BATCH_PROCESSING_TIME
│   └── It should revert with ExitQueueRequestCannotBeClosed
├── Given batch is priced but MAX_BATCH_PROCESSING_TIME exceeded
│   ├── It should call exitQueue.closeRequest() (escape hatch)
│   ├── It should refund tokens to user (via safeTransfer)
│   └── It should emit RedemptionCancelled event with viaEscapeHatch == true
└── Given batch is not priced (valid cancellation)
    ├── It should call exitQueue.closeRequest()
    ├── It should refund tokens to user (via safeTransfer)
    └── It should emit RedemptionCancelled event with viaEscapeHatch == false

AMM::freeBalance()
├── Given no pending claims (lockedForClaims == 0)
│   └── It should return address(this).balance
└── Given pending claims exist (lockedForClaims > 0)
    ├── It should return address(this).balance - lockedForClaims
    └── It should route a new exit to the queue when free balance is fully locked

AMM::setConnectorWeight(uint256 _cw)
├── Given caller does not have ADMIN_ROLE
│   └── It should revert with AccessControlUnauthorizedAccount
├── When connector weight is zero
│   └── It should revert with AMMInvalidRange
├── When connector weight is greater than Math.SCALE_FACTOR (1e18)
│   └── It should revert with AMMInvalidRange
└── Given valid connector weight
    ├── It should update connectorWeight
    └── It should emit ConnectorWeightChanged event

AMM::setMinBatchExitETH(uint256 _minBatchExitETH)
├── Given caller does not have ADMIN_ROLE
│   └── It should revert with AccessControlUnauthorizedAccount
├── Given _minBatchExitETH exceeds MIN_BATCH_EXIT_ETH_UPPER_BOUND
│   └── It should revert with AMMInvalidMinBatchExitETH
├── Given valid parameters
│   ├── It should update minBatchExitETH
│   └── It should emit MinBatchExitETHChanged event
├── Given _minBatchExitETH equals MIN_BATCH_EXIT_ETH_UPPER_BOUND
│   └── It should update minBatchExitETH to the upper bound
├── Given _minBatchExitETH is zero
│   └── It should disable the batch exit minimum check
└── Given contract is paused
    └── It should still succeed (function doesn't check pause)

AMM::pause()
├── Given caller has neither ADMIN_ROLE nor SECURITY_ROLE on Registry
│   └── It should revert with RegistryClientCallerHasNoneOfRoles
├── Given caller has SECURITY_ROLE on Registry
│   └── It should pause the contract immediately (no timelock)
├── Given contract is not paused
│   ├── It should pause the contract
│   └── It should emit Paused event
└── Given contract is already paused
    └── It should revert with EnforcedPause

AMM::unpause()
├── Given caller does not have ADMIN_ROLE
│   └── It should revert with AccessControlUnauthorizedAccount
└── Given caller has ADMIN_ROLE and contract is paused
    ├── It should unpause the contract (paused() == false)
    └── It should resume enter/exit operations

AMM::evePremiumPriceInETH()
├── Given total supply is zero
│   └── It should revert with AMMZeroTotalSupply
└── Given valid state
    ├── It should match formula: (liveNAV * NORMALIZATION_FACTOR) / (liveSupply * cw / SCALE_FACTOR)
    ├── It should use totalNAVInETH() (strategies + controller + AMM free balance − in-window priced liability)
    └── It should use liveSupply = totalSupply − in-window priced escrow (unpriced queued EVE stays in)

AMM::eveBasePriceInETH()
└── Given valid state
    ├── It should match formula: (liveNAV * NORMALIZATION_FACTOR) / liveSupply
    ├── It should use totalNAVInETH() (strategies + controller + AMM free balance − in-window priced liability)
    └── It should use liveSupply = totalSupply − in-window priced escrow (unpriced queued EVE stays in)

AMM::evePremiumPriceInUSD()
├── Given total supply is zero
│   └── It should revert with AMMZeroTotalSupply
└── Given valid state
    ├── It should equal evePremiumPriceInETH() converted via oracle.convertTokenToUSD
    └── It should always be >= eveBasePriceInUSD()

AMM::eveBasePriceInUSD()
├── Given total supply is zero
│   └── It should revert with AMMZeroTotalSupply
├── Given oracle price is stale
│   └── It should revert
└── Given valid state
    ├── It should match formula: totalNAVInUSD() * NORMALIZATION_FACTOR / liveSupply
    └── It should equal eveBasePriceInETH() converted via oracle.convertTokenToUSD

AMM::Pricing & NAV (ETH-first)
├── Given enter/exit use ETH prices (not USD)
│   ├── enter() should price tokens via evePremiumPriceInETH()
│   └── exit() should size the burn via eveBasePriceInETH()
├── Given connector weight changes
│   └── Premium price should decrease as connector weight increases (and stay >= base price)
├── Given NAV includes AMM free balance
│   ├── totalNAVInETH() should equal controller balance + AMM freeBalance() (no strategies)
│   └── base/premium ETH prices should reflect AMM free balance in NAV
├── Given ETH locked for pending claims (after processRedemption)
│   ├── totalNAVInETH() should use AMM freeBalance() only (exclude lockedForClaims)
│   └── enter premium price should not be inflated by locked claim ETH
├── Given an in-window priced ExitQueue batch
│   ├── totalNAVInETH() should deduct liabilityETH (remainingTokens * finalEvePrice)
│   ├── eveBasePriceInETH() / evePremiumPriceInETH() should use liveSupply (exclude escrowed EVE)
│   └── unpriced queued EVE should remain in the supply denominator (cancellable equity)
├── Given the priced batch is past MAX_BATCH_PROCESSING_TIME
│   ├── liveRedemptionOffsets should return (0, 0) with no write (liability lapses on the clock)
│   └── pullRequest / processRedemption should revert with ExitQueueBatchExpired
├── Given prices recomputed after operations
│   ├── ETH prices should follow NAV/supply and change after enter
│   └── USD prices should remain oracle conversions of ETH prices
└── Given zero NAV
    └── eveBasePriceInETH() should be zero when NAV is zero

AMM::initialize / immutability
├── Given freshly constructed AMM
│   ├── controller() should equal the controller address
│   ├── MIN_INITIAL_DEPOSIT_USD() should equal 1000e18
│   └── connectorWeight() should equal the initial connector weight
└── Given AMM is immutable (no upgrade path)
    └── controller(), connectorWeight(), and eve() should remain stable

AMM::pause behavior
├── Given contract is paused
│   ├── enter() should revert with EnforcedPause
│   ├── exit() should revert with EnforcedPause
│   └── View functions (paused, controller, connectorWeight, price views) should still work
└── Given contract is unpaused again
    └── enter() should work

AMM::Large NAV moves (deviation guard removed in #241)
├── Given bootstrap and a large enter land in the same block
│   └── It should not freeze — next-block enter and immediate exit work (M-1 regression)
├── Given NAV jumps far beyond the old 5% band (e.g. harvest yield accrual)
│   └── It should price enter/exit against the new NAV without freezing (M-2 regression)
└── Given NAV drops sharply (realized strategy loss)
    └── It should price enter/exit against the new NAV (user slippage params are the protection)

AMM::Fuzz Testing
├── testFuzz_Enter_WithValidAmounts
│   └── It should bootstrap and mint EVE for valid ETH deposits
├── testFuzz_ExitWithValidAmounts
│   └── It should process immediate redemption for valid ETH requests within user balance
├── testFuzz_SetConnectorWeight
│   └── It should set connectorWeight for any value in (0, 1e18]
└── testFuzz_ConnectorWeight
    └── It should accept any connector weight in (0, 1e18]
